.TH "ELSERENO" "1" "2026\-04\-26" "ElSereno user commands" "Commands"
.SH NAME
\f[B]elsereno\f[R]: ICS/OT and legacy\-network exposure auditor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]elsereno\f[R] [\f[B]\-\-config\f[R] \f[I]file\f[R]]
[\f[B]\-\-dry\-run\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-format\f[R] \f[I]fmt\f[R]]
\f[I]command\f[R] [\f[I]args\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]ElSereno\f[R] scans for and audits exposure of legacy + ICS / OT
network protocols (Modbus, S7, EtherNet/IP, BACnet, DNP3, IEC
60870\-5\-104, HART\-IP, Niagara Fox, OPC UA, ATG, XOT, AT modems,
banner / dictionary, plus PBX SIP / IAX2 / pbxhttp / TR\-069 CWMP).
Two binaries ship from the same module:
.TP
\f[B]elsereno\f[R]
Default (read\-only) build.
Scan, fingerprint, score, triage, serve dashboard.
Writes refused at the wire layer.
.TP
\f[B]elsereno\-offensive\f[R]
\f[CR]\-tags offensive\f[R] build.
Adds \f[B]dial\f[R], \f[B]exploit\f[R], \f[B]harvest\f[R], \f[B]proxy
listen\f[R] (write\-gated), and \f[B]write\f[R] subcommands.
Every mutating call clears the triple\-confirm wrapper (ADR\-039),
\f[CR]\-\-accept\-writes\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-confirm\-target\f[R],
\f[CR]\-\-confirm\-token\f[R].
.SH COMMANDS
The default\-build subcommand list is below.
Run \f[CR]elsereno *command* \-\-help\f[R] for per\-command flags.
.TP
\f[B]api\f[R]
HTTP API meta\-operations.
\f[CR]api openapi\f[R] prints the live OpenAPI 3.1 spec.
.TP
\f[B]audit\f[R]
Audit\-chain operations on \f[CR]\(ti/.elsereno/audit.jsonl\f[R]:
\f[B]verify\-file\f[R] walks the chain, \f[B]export\f[R] writes events
for a SIEM (ndjson, cef, syslog), \f[B]serve\f[R] runs the fan\-in
daemon on a Unix socket.
\f[B]verify\f[R], \f[B]purge\f[R] and \f[B]compact\f[R] check their
flags and then do nothing yet (exit 69).
.TP
\f[B]backup\f[R]
Encrypted backup + restore (vault\-keyed AES\-256\-GCM).
.TP
\f[B]completion\f[R]
Generate shell completions (placeholder; see \f[CR]\-\-help\f[R] until
cobra\(aqs generator is wired).
.TP
\f[B]config\f[R]
Inspect and validate configuration: \f[B]show\f[R], \f[B]lint\f[R].
(Canonical formatting is the top\-level \f[B]fmt\f[R].)
.TP
\f[B]creds\f[R]
Manage stored credentials inside the vault.
.TP
\f[B]db\f[R]
Database operations: \f[B]migrate up/down\f[R], \f[B]status\f[R],
\f[B]verify\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]doctor\f[R]
Run six local preflight checks: Go runtime, platform, raw\-socket
privilege, nmap on PATH, IPv6, free disk.
Neither root nor nmap is needed to scan; reads no config, vault or
database.
.TP
\f[B]explain\f[R]
Explain how a finding\(aqs score was computed (ADR\-006 factors).
.TP
\f[B]fingerprint\f[R]
Debug one plugin: \f[B]probe\f[R] a live host:port, \f[B]capture\f[R]
one TCP connection\(aqs bytes to a file, \f[B]validate\f[R] a plugin
against captured bytes (offline).
.TP
\f[B]fmt\f[R]
Re\-emit a YAML config with canonical formatting.
.TP
\f[B]goose\f[R]
IEC 61850 GOOSE/SV dissector, offline: \f[B]decode\f[R] one frame,
\f[B]monitor\f[R] a frame stream for spoofing signs; \f[B]monitor
\-\-iface\f[R] reads a receive\-only AF_PACKET socket on Linux
(CAP_NET_RAW).
.TP
\f[B]gen\-man\f[R]
Generate man1 pages via cobra/doc (placeholder; current man1 lives under
\f[CR]man/src/man1/*.md\f[R]).
.TP
\f[B]legal\f[R]
Print the acceptable\-use policy disclaimer.
.TP
\f[B]lint\f[R]
Validate \f[B]elsereno.yaml\f[R] and optional \f[B]scope.yaml\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]modbus\f[R]
\f[B]modbus monitor \-\-file\f[R]: passive, offline; reports the writes
and mutating diagnostics in a Modbus/TCP frame stream (one hex frame per
line).
.TP
\f[B]opcua\f[R]
Read\-only OPC UA recon: \f[B]probe\-anon\f[R] confirms an anonymous
session opens; \f[B]probe\-write\f[R] walks the address space as that
user and flags writeable tags.
.TP
\f[B]plaintext\-check\f[R]
Tests whether a reachable service negotiates TLS; one that does not is
flagged as cleartext.
.TP
\f[B]plugins\f[R]
Manage protocol plugins.
\f[B]plugins list\f[R] prints the compiled\-in set (35 in the default
build).
.TP
\f[B]discover\f[R]
\f[CR]discover \-\-auto <CIDR>\f[R] runs a TCP\-connect sweep across the
CIDR + the well\-known port of every registered plugin.
Pipe\-friendly: \f[CR]\-\-format list\f[R] emits \f[CR]host:port\f[R]
lines for \f[CR]scan \-\-input list:\-\f[R] (\f[CR]list:\-\f[R] reads
stdin).
.TP
\f[B]profinet\f[R]
PROFINET DCP codec, offline: \f[B]decode\f[R] a frame,
\f[B]encode\-identify\f[R] prints an Identify\-All request.
.TP
\f[B]proxy\f[R]
Protocol\-aware interception proxy.
\f[B]proxy listen\f[R] runs a write\-gated proxy in the offensive build.
In the default build \f[B]proxy\f[R] is a stub that exits 75 (planned):
the per\-plugin handlers that refuse writes (write\-ban, deny\-all,
fail\-closed) exist as library code, but no command serves them yet.
.TP
\f[B]scan\f[R]
Scan a set of targets and emit findings.
\f[CR]\-\-input <provider>:<query>\f[R] accepts \f[CR]list:\f[R],
\f[CR]nmap:\f[R], \f[CR]stdin\f[R], \f[CR]shodan:\f[R],
\f[CR]censys:\f[R], \f[CR]fofa:\f[R], \f[CR]zoomeye:\f[R],
\f[CR]onyphe:\f[R], \f[CR]binaryedge:\f[R], \f[CR]internetdb:\f[R].
\f[B]shodan\f[R], \f[B]censys\f[R], \f[B]fofa\f[R], \f[B]zoomeye\f[R],
\f[B]onyphe\f[R] and \f[B]binaryedge\f[R] need
\f[CR]\-\-api\-creds\-file <0600.yaml>\f[R]; \f[B]internetdb\f[R] needs
no key and takes an IP, \f[CR]file:<path>\f[R] or \f[CR]\-\f[R] (no
CIDR).
Each target goes to every plugin whose default port it is on
(\f[B]banner\f[R] probes every target; opt\-in plugins run only when
named, and then probe every listed target, having no default port);
\f[CR]\-\-plugin <name>[,<name>]\f[R] restricts the set.
Each finding carries the target\(aqs address and port.
\f[CR]\-\-output\-format\f[R] accepts \f[CR]ndjson\f[R], \f[CR]csv\f[R]
and \f[CR]stix\f[R] (STIX 2.1 bundle for MISP / OpenCTI / ThreatBus,
v1.15+); \f[CR]\-\-output <file>\f[R] writes to a file instead of
stdout.
To probe one plugin on another port, use \f[B]fingerprint probe\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]s7\f[R]
Read\-only S7comm recon of a Siemens CPU: \f[B]probe\-identity\f[R]
(model, firmware), \f[B]probe\-protection\f[R] (protection level),
\f[B]probe\f[R] (both).
.TP
\f[B]schedule\f[R]
Manage scheduled scans through a running \f[B]serve\f[R]
(\f[B]list\f[R], \f[B]get\f[R], \f[B]enable\f[R], \f[B]disable\f[R],
\f[B]delete\f[R], \f[B]clone\f[R], \f[B]import\f[R], \f[B]export\f[R],
\f[B]pause\-all\f[R], \f[B]resume\-all\f[R], \f[B]stats\f[R]).
.TP
\f[B]scoring\f[R]
Inspect the scoring weights and severity thresholds.
.TP
\f[B]serve\f[R]
Start the HTTP dashboard at the configured listen address + serve
\f[CR]/api/v1\f[R].
With \f[B]\-\-scan\-store\f[R] memory or db, scans queued from the
dashboard, the API or a schedule run against their targets (limited by
\f[B]\-\-scope\f[R] when given); jobs already queued when serve starts
do not run.
Findings go to the SSE stream and, with \f[B]DATABASE_URL\f[R], to the
runs and findings tables.
.TP
\f[B]standards\f[R]
Prints the mapping from plugins to the security\-standard weaknesses
their findings evidence (NIST SP 800\-82 Rev.
4).
.TP
\f[B]triage\f[R]
Group NDJSON findings into quick\-win / strategic / routine.
.TP
\f[B]tui\f[R]
Interactive terminal UI: empty panes, \f[B]\-\-input\f[R] (scan from the
TUI), \f[B]\-\-replay\f[R] a recorded NDJSON, \f[B]\-\-feed \-\f[R] from
stdin, or \f[B]\-\-watch\f[R] a remote SSE stream.
.TP
\f[B]vault\f[R]
Manage the encrypted credential vault: \f[B]init\f[R], \f[B]unlock\f[R],
\f[B]lock\f[R], \f[B]status\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]version\f[R]
Print binary version, commit, and build date.
.TP
\f[B]why\f[R]
Explain the scoring posture for a target.
.TP
\f[B]diff\f[R], \f[B]init\f[R], \f[B]repl\f[R], \f[B]token\f[R]
Planned: each exits 75 with a notice on stderr.
.SH OFFENSIVE\-ONLY COMMANDS
The \f[CR]\-tags offensive\f[R] build adds:
.TP
\f[B]dial\f[R]
Dial guard (ADR\-041).
Subcommands: \f[B]validate\f[R] (single number) and \f[B]batch\f[R]
(wardialing batch with \f[CR]\-\-numbers\-file\f[R]).
.TP
\f[B]exploit\f[R]
CVE exploit catalogue.
\f[B]exploit list\f[R] + \f[B]exploit dry\-run\f[R]
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]exploit run\f[R].
.RE
.TP
\f[B]harvest\f[R]
Credential harvest probes (telnet / ftp / http\-basic / snmp).
.TP
\f[B]write\f[R]
Protocol\-specific write operations.
Per\-protocol subcommands: \f[B]modbus dry\-run\f[R], \f[B]modbus
send\f[R], \f[B]modbus proxy\-dry\-run\f[R], \f[B]sip dry\-run\f[R],
\f[B]iax2 dry\-run\f[R], \f[B]pbxhttp dry\-run\f[R], \f[B]opcua
dry\-run\f[R], \f[B]bacnet dry\-run\f[R], \f[B]cwmp dry\-run\f[R].
.SH WRITE\-GATE FLAGS (offensive build)
Seven of the 18 write\-gated proxies accept the
\f[CR]\-\-allow\-file <path.yaml>\f[R] round\-trip flow.
Direct CLI flags per proxy:
.TP
\f[B]Modbus\f[R]
\f[CR]\-\-function <FC>\f[R],
\f[CR]\-\-write unit=N;fc=M;start=A;end=B\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]OPC UA\f[R]
\f[CR]\-\-service <TypeID>\f[R],
\f[CR]\-\-node\-id ns=N;i=M|s=STR|g=HEX|b=HEX\f[R],
\f[CR]\-\-call\-method object=\&...;method=\&...\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]SIP\f[R]
\f[CR]\-\-method <NAME>\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-to\-prefix <prefix>\f[R],
\f[CR]\-\-aor <AOR>\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-from\-domain <host>\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]IAX2\f[R]
\f[CR]\-\-subclass <NAME>\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]pbxhttp\f[R]
\f[CR]\-\-allow METHOD:/path\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]BACnet\f[R]
\f[CR]\-\-service\-choice <N>\f[R],
\f[CR]\-\-object type=N;instance=M;property=P\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]CWMP\f[R]
\f[CR]\-\-rpc <Name>\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-param\-prefix <prefix>\f[R],
\f[CR]\-\-firmware url=\&...;sha256=\&...\f[R].
.SH GLOBAL FLAGS
.TP
\f[B]\-\-config\f[R] \f[I]file\f[R]
Path to \f[CR]elsereno.yaml\f[R] (overrides default lookup order).
.TP
\f[B]\-\-dry\-run\f[R]
Simulate side effects without performing them.
Only \f[B]schedule delete\f[R], \f[B]enable\f[R], \f[B]disable\f[R],
\f[B]clone\f[R], \f[B]import\f[R], \f[B]pause\-all\f[R] and
\f[B]resume\-all\f[R] implement it; every other command refuses to run
with it (exit 64) instead of acting.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-format\f[R] \f[I]yaml|json|table|ndjson|csv\f[R]
Output format selector (per\-command support varies).
.TP
\f[B]\-\-quiet\f[R] (offensive\-build only)
Suppress non\-critical output.
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[CR]\(ti/.elsereno/vault.v1.bin\f[R]
AES\-GCM + Argon2id vault.
.TP
\f[CR]\(ti/.elsereno/audit.jsonl\f[R]
JCS+SHA\-256 audit chain (0600).
.TP
\f[CR]\(ti/.elsereno/dev.pp\f[R]
Operator\-supplied passphrase file (0600).
Pass via \f[CR]\-\-vault\-passphrase\-file\f[R].
.TP
\f[CR]\(ti/.elsereno/api\-creds.yaml\f[R]
Provider API keys for \f[CR]\-\-input <provider>:<q>\f[R].
0600 enforced at load.
.TP
\f[CR]./elsereno.yaml\f[R]
Per\-project config, last in the lookup order (see
\f[I]elsereno.yaml\f[R](5)).
A \f[I]scope.yaml\f[R] is read only when passed with
\f[B]\-\-scope\f[R], which every command that connects to a target
accepts (\f[I]elsereno\-scope\f[R](5)).
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
\f[CR]0\f[R]
success.
.TP
\f[CR]1\f[R]
error (also an unknown flag or a missing argument).
.TP
\f[CR]64\f[R]
usage error, \f[I]EX_USAGE\f[R] (also a name given as
\f[B]\-\-target\f[R] to a write\-class verb with \f[B]\-\-scope\f[R]).
.TP
\f[CR]66\f[R]
nothing left to do, \f[I]EX_NOINPUT\f[R] (no targets after the scope
filter).
.TP
\f[CR]68\f[R]
a \f[B]\-\-target\f[R] name that does not resolve, \f[I]EX_NOHOST\f[R]:
with \f[B]\-\-scope\f[R], and always in \f[B]fingerprint probe\f[R].
.TP
\f[CR]77\f[R]
refused by \f[B]\-\-scope\f[R], \f[I]EX_NOPERM\f[R]: a target outside
its ranges or ports, or a plugin outside its protocols.
.TP
\f[CR]78\f[R]
configuration error, \f[I]EX_CONFIG\f[R]: a config or scope file that
does not parse.
.TP
\f[CR]128 + signum\f[R]
killed by a signal (e.g.
SIGINT → \f[B]130\f[R], SIGTERM → \f[B]143\f[R]).
.TP
\f[CR]75\f[R]
\f[I]EX_TEMPFAIL\f[R]: emitted by the verbs that are still stubs
(planned for a later phase, \f[B]proxy\f[R] in the default build among
them) and by \f[CR]proxy listen\f[R] (offensive build) on SIGHUP.
Distinguishable from a real crash via systemd\(aqs
\f[CR]RestartPreventExitStatus=\f[R]; supervisor restarts with the new
allowlist + freshly minted confirm\-token (v1.15+).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\f[B]ELSERENO_VAULT_PASSPHRASE\f[R]
Emits a warning when a TTY is present; prefer \f[CR]vault unlock\f[R] or
a 0600 file.
.TP
\f[B]DATABASE_URL\f[R]
Postgres DSN.
Optional; missing → DB\-backed panels degrade to \(dqbackend
unavailable\(dq, dashboard scans keep their findings only on the live
stream, and the rest of \f[CR]serve\f[R] keeps running.
